------Cloud computing basics - 
------- Iaas = Infrastructure as a service, Gives full control over infra resources such as virtual machine/storage etc, You must take care of all the Admin tasks such as patching, upgrades, backups.Pay-per-use, EC2, VM, GCE
Ideal choice for life and shift migration and legacy application.
------- Paas = Platform as a service, give runtime environment/platform to deploy application and development tools, Azure takes care of all the admin tasks including automated backups
Pay-per-service model, Azure web app,Ideal choice where customer doesn't want to take care of Admin tasks
------- Saas = Software as a service, gives application access to the end users, Azure takes care of all the admin tasks.
Pay-per-subscription model, 0365, Gmail, Dropbox etc, Ideal choice where customer can use the standard version of a cloud application.

------- Public Cloud: Resources are shared among multiple users, owned by third-party providers like AWS or Azure, and operate on a pay-as-you-go basis with low upfront costs.
------- Private Cloud: Dedicated entirely to a single organization, offering enhanced control and security but requiring high upfront investment for hardware.
------- Hybrid Cloud: Combines public and private clouds, allowing organizations to securely manage sensitive data on-premises while leveraging public cloud scalability for other needs

------vocabulary
virtualization     =  the technology that allows one physical computer to run multiple virtual computers (called virtual machines) simultaneously. each virtual machines behaves like a separte, independate computer. this is the foundation of cloud computing.
virtual machines   = a software based computer that runs ona physucal host computer. it has its own operating system, cpu, memory, and storage, but shares the underlying physical hardware. you can create, delete, resize vms in seconds on the cloud.
api                = application programming interface. A set of rules and protocols that allows different software applications to communicate with each other. In cloud computing api's let your app talk to the cloud services(like requestingstorage or starting a VM) without knowing their internal details, like a waiter in a restaurant you give the order(request to the waiter(api) and the kitchen(cloud service) prepares it for you.
regions            = geohraphic areas where cloud providers have data centers. each region is a seprate geographich area(e.g., "US East", "Europe west", "Asia south"). Choosing a region close to your users reduces latency(loading time).
Availability zones = Isolated data centres locations within a region, each with independent power, cooling and networking. if one zone fails (e.g., due to a power outage), others continue running.Deploying across multiple aones makes your app more reliable.
Scalability        = the ability tpo increase(scale up/out) or decrease(scale down/in) computing resources based on demand. Vertical scaling = adding more power to one machine. Horizontal scaling = adding more machines.
Elasticity         = the ability to automatically scale resources up or down in real time based on current demand - eithout hunan interventions. it is scalability done automatically. you pay only for what you use.
agility            = the ability to rapidly develop, tesst, and deploy applications in the cloud. Cloud agility means you can set up new resources in minutes instead of weeks, allowing faster innovation and response to business changes.
High availablility = A design approach that ensures a systrm remains operational and accessible fpr the maximum possible time - typically 99.9% or higher uptime. Axgieved by eliminating single points of failure, redundancy,  and running across multiple availability zones.
Fault tolerance    = The ability of a system to continue operating correctly even when one or more of its components fail. Unlike high availability(which minimizes downtime), fault tolerance means zero downtime - the system works even during a failure.
Disaster recovery  = a set of policies and procedures to recover data and restore systems after a catastrophic event ( fire, cyberattack, natural disaster). In the cloud, this involves backing up data in different regions and having a plan to restore services quickly.
Load Balancing     = the process of distributing incoming network traffic evenly across multiple servers so no single server is overwhelmed. This improves responsiveness and availability. A load balanves sits in front of your servers and routes requests intelligently.

