------Jenkins is an open-source CI/CD automation tool used to automate software building, testing, and deployment processes. It helps automate workflows such as integrating code from GitHub, running tests, and deploying applications to servers or cloud platforms like Azure and AWS.
------ CI = Continuous Integration
Means:
developers continuously add code changes to a shared repository (like GitHub).
When code is pushed:
app builds automatically
tests run automatically
issues are detected early

------- CD = Continuous Deployment / Delivery
Means:
after testing,
the application gets:
deployed automatically
OR
prepared for deployment
to:
cloud
servers
production environment

